WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:06.765
Here are three claims about whole numbers.

2
00:00:06.765 --> 00:00:09.709
One: if n is a multiple of six

3
00:00:09.709 --> 00:00:12.562
then n is a multiple of three.

4
00:00:12.562 --> 00:00:15.691
Two: if n is a multiple of three

5
00:00:15.691 --> 00:00:18.359
then n is a multiple of six.

6
00:00:18.359 --> 00:00:22.500
Three: if n squared is even, then n is even.

7
00:00:22.850 --> 00:00:25.211
A computer tests all three

8
00:00:25.211 --> 00:00:27.747
for n from one to a hundred.

9
00:00:27.747 --> 00:00:30.807
Claim two fails at n equals three.

10
00:00:30.807 --> 00:00:34.130
Claims one and three pass every test.

11
00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:38.372
So are claims one and three now theorems?

12
00:00:38.372 --> 00:00:40.080
Pause and decide.

13
00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:44.327
Not yet.

14
00:00:44.327 --> 00:00:47.913
A hundred tests are not a hundred percent

15
00:00:47.913 --> 00:00:51.332
the next number could break the pattern.

16
00:00:51.416 --> 00:00:53.834
A theorem is a statement that

17
00:00:53.917 --> 00:00:57.420
is true in every case, with no exceptions.

18
00:00:57.770 --> 00:01:01.100
A proof is the argument that shows it.

19
00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:04.604
Each step follows from the definitions

20
00:01:04.604 --> 00:01:06.444
from what we assume

21
00:01:06.444 --> 00:01:09.160
or from results proved before.

22
00:01:09.160 --> 00:01:12.402
One proof covers every case at once

23
00:01:12.402 --> 00:01:16.170
even the ones no computer will ever reach.

24
00:01:16.750 --> 00:01:19.807
Most theorems say: if A, then B.

25
00:01:19.807 --> 00:01:21.814
A is the hypothesis

26
00:01:21.814 --> 00:01:24.202
and B is the conclusion.

27
00:01:24.202 --> 00:01:27.546
We also say A is sufficient for B

28
00:01:27.546 --> 00:01:30.030
and B is necessary for A.

29
00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:34.601
Now sort numbers by two questions.

30
00:01:34.601 --> 00:01:37.581
Is n a multiple of six?

31
00:01:37.581 --> 00:01:38.946
That is A.

32
00:01:38.946 --> 00:01:42.174
Is n a multiple of three?

33
00:01:42.174 --> 00:01:43.540
That is B.

34
00:01:43.540 --> 00:01:49.127
Six, twelve and eighteen land here: A and B.

35
00:01:49.127 --> 00:01:53.845
Three, nine and fifteen: B without A.

36
00:01:53.845 --> 00:01:56.700
All the rest: neither.

37
00:01:57.050 --> 00:02:00.950
One cell stays empty: A true and B false.

38
00:02:00.950 --> 00:02:04.374
That empty cell is the whole claim.

39
00:02:04.469 --> 00:02:07.322
An if-then statement is broken

40
00:02:07.417 --> 00:02:09.890
only by that kind of case.

41
00:02:10.470 --> 00:02:13.170
To prove that the cell stays

42
00:02:13.267 --> 00:02:16.931
empty for every n, use a direct proof.

43
00:02:16.931 --> 00:02:20.210
Assume A: n is a multiple of six

44
00:02:20.210 --> 00:02:24.550
so n equals six times a, for some integer a.

45
00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:28.637
Then n equals three times two a

46
00:02:28.637 --> 00:02:33.893
and two a is an integer, so three divides n.

47
00:02:33.893 --> 00:02:35.177
That is B.

48
00:02:35.177 --> 00:02:37.980
Claim one is a theorem.

49
00:02:38.330 --> 00:02:41.963
The same pattern proves: if n is odd

50
00:02:41.963 --> 00:02:44.221
then n squared is odd.

51
00:02:44.221 --> 00:02:46.872
Write n as two a plus one.

52
00:02:46.872 --> 00:02:49.719
Then n squared is two times

53
00:02:49.719 --> 00:02:53.254
two a squared plus two a, plus one.

54
00:02:53.254 --> 00:02:54.530
That is odd.

55
00:02:55.110 --> 00:02:58.836
Swap the hypothesis and the conclusion

56
00:02:58.836 --> 00:03:02.658
and you get the converse: if B, then A.

57
00:03:02.658 --> 00:03:05.428
If n is a multiple of three

58
00:03:05.428 --> 00:03:08.199
then n is a multiple of six.

59
00:03:08.199 --> 00:03:10.110
That was claim two.

60
00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:14.636
The converse is broken by a different cell

61
00:03:14.636 --> 00:03:16.675
B true, but A false.

62
00:03:16.675 --> 00:03:21.045
And that cell is full: three, nine, fifteen.

63
00:03:21.045 --> 00:03:23.570
So the converse is false

64
00:03:23.570 --> 00:03:26.580
even though the claim is true.

65
00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:30.790
Now negate both parts and swap them

66
00:03:30.790 --> 00:03:33.009
if not B, then not A.

67
00:03:33.009 --> 00:03:35.833
This is the contrapositive.

68
00:03:35.833 --> 00:03:38.656
If three does not divide n

69
00:03:38.656 --> 00:03:41.480
then six does not divide n.

70
00:03:41.830 --> 00:03:43.998
Which case breaks it?

71
00:03:43.998 --> 00:03:46.991
Not B true, and not A false.

72
00:03:46.991 --> 00:03:50.190
That means B false and A true

73
00:03:50.190 --> 00:03:53.390
the same empty cell as before.

74
00:03:53.740 --> 00:03:56.501
So a statement and its contrapositive

75
00:03:56.575 --> 00:03:58.739
are broken by the same cases.

76
00:03:58.739 --> 00:04:01.947
They are true together and false together.

77
00:04:01.947 --> 00:04:04.260
They are logically equivalent.

78
00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:07.828
That gives a second way to prove things.

79
00:04:07.828 --> 00:04:09.599
To prove claim three

80
00:04:09.599 --> 00:04:12.576
if n squared is even then n is even

81
00:04:12.576 --> 00:04:15.713
prove its contrapositive: if n is odd

82
00:04:15.713 --> 00:04:17.564
then n squared is odd.

83
00:04:17.564 --> 00:04:18.610
We just did.

84
00:04:19.190 --> 00:04:22.446
To show that a claim is false

85
00:04:22.446 --> 00:04:25.702
one counterexample is enough.

86
00:04:25.702 --> 00:04:30.151
Claim: if p is prime, then two to the p

87
00:04:30.151 --> 00:04:32.430
minus one, is prime.

88
00:04:32.780 --> 00:04:36.749
Two, three, five and seven give three

89
00:04:36.749 --> 00:04:37.480
seven

90
00:04:37.480 --> 00:04:41.761
thirty-one and one hundred twenty-seven.

91
00:04:41.761 --> 00:04:42.910
All prime.

92
00:04:43.014 --> 00:04:46.043
But eleven gives two thousand

93
00:04:46.147 --> 00:04:47.818
and forty-seven

94
00:04:47.818 --> 00:04:52.100
which is twenty-three times eighty-nine.

95
00:04:52.450 --> 00:04:55.865
Eleven is prime, and the result is not

96
00:04:55.865 --> 00:04:57.967
the hypothesis is true

97
00:04:57.967 --> 00:05:00.506
and the conclusion is false.

98
00:05:00.506 --> 00:05:02.170
The claim is dead.

99
00:05:02.520 --> 00:05:04.777
What about p equals four?

100
00:05:04.777 --> 00:05:08.387
Two to the four, minus one, is fifteen

101
00:05:08.387 --> 00:05:10.193
which is not prime.

102
00:05:10.193 --> 00:05:12.901
But four is not prime either.

103
00:05:12.901 --> 00:05:16.421
The claim promised nothing about four

104
00:05:16.421 --> 00:05:19.400
so four is not a counterexample.

105
00:05:19.980 --> 00:05:22.173
Last, if and only if.

106
00:05:22.173 --> 00:05:26.559
A if and only if B means both directions

107
00:05:26.559 --> 00:05:29.692
A implies B, and B implies A.

108
00:05:29.692 --> 00:05:33.660
So both of these cells must be empty.

109
00:05:34.010 --> 00:05:35.268
For example

110
00:05:35.268 --> 00:05:39.880
n is even if and only if n squared is even.

111
00:05:39.880 --> 00:05:42.396
Forward: if n is two a

112
00:05:42.396 --> 00:05:46.904
then n squared is two times two a squared.

113
00:05:46.904 --> 00:05:49.525
Backward is claim three

114
00:05:49.525 --> 00:05:52.250
proved by contrapositive.

115
00:05:52.600 --> 00:05:55.130
One failed direction is enough

116
00:05:55.214 --> 00:05:57.406
to kill an if and only if.

117
00:05:57.406 --> 00:06:00.105
Is x squared greater than four

118
00:06:00.105 --> 00:06:03.309
if and only if x is greater than two?

119
00:06:03.309 --> 00:06:04.826
Take minus three.

120
00:06:04.826 --> 00:06:07.103
Nine is greater than four

121
00:06:07.103 --> 00:06:10.560
but minus three is not greater than two.

122
00:06:11.140 --> 00:06:12.093
To sum up.

123
00:06:12.188 --> 00:06:14.666
If A then B is broken only

124
00:06:14.761 --> 00:06:16.857
by A true and B false.

125
00:06:16.953 --> 00:06:19.621
The contrapositive is broken

126
00:06:19.716 --> 00:06:23.337
by the same case, so it is equivalent.

127
00:06:23.337 --> 00:06:25.338
The converse is not.

128
00:06:25.338 --> 00:06:29.340
And one counterexample disproves a claim.

129
00:06:29.920 --> 00:06:33.902
Try it yourself: write the converse and the

130
00:06:33.994 --> 00:06:35.661
contrapositive of

131
00:06:35.661 --> 00:06:39.736
if n is a multiple of four, then n is even.

132
00:06:39.736 --> 00:06:41.680
Which ones are true?

133
00:06:42.030 --> 00:06:45.079
In part two, true and false become an

134
00:06:45.161 --> 00:06:46.892
algebra of their own

135
00:06:46.892 --> 00:06:50.270
with truth tables that check every case.
